course: dictionary
lesson: 3870
title: Words from the Bible and the world
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A noun names a thing, a person or a place. Frankincense is a noun. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Wise men from the East brought gold, frankincense and myrrh.» Gold and myrrh are gifts, so frankincense is probably a gift too.
explain: «Saba was a real kingdom in what is now Yemen, rich from trading frankincense and myrrh.» Rich from trading means people sold frankincense to get wealth. Ask yourself what word would fit in the sentence, then try your meaning in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some words have a special meaning in one subject, such as church or the Bible. In the Bible story, frankincense is one of the three gifts for baby Jesus. Its meaning there is different from the meaning you would find in a science book about tree sap.
fact: Frankincense is a noun.
fact: «Frankincense» means a sweet-smelling gum, or resin, from certain trees in Arabia and Africa, burned to make perfumed smoke.
fact: In the Bible, frankincense was one of three gifts the wise men gave baby Jesus, with gold and myrrh.
fact: Christians see frankincense as a sign that Jesus is God, since it was burned in worship.
fact: The Bible does not say there were three wise men, only that there were three gifts.
exercise: «Wise men from the East brought gold, frankincense and myrrh.» What is frankincense here? | *A sweet-smelling gum from trees, given as a gift | A type of star | A king from Egypt | A kind of gold coin
exercise: «Saba was rich from trading frankincense and myrrh.» What were frankincense and myrrh? | Metals dug from the ground | *Sweet-smelling tree gums | Stone ships | Woven cloth
exercise: Christians see frankincense as a sign that Jesus is | a shepherd | a rich merchant | *God | a king
test: The Bible tells us there were three gifts. How many wise men does it say there were? | Two | Three, because there were three gifts | Twelve | *It does not say how many
test: What part of speech is «frankincense»? | adjective | adverb | verb | *noun
exam: In «gold, frankincense and myrrh», what is frankincense? | *a sweet-smelling gum from trees | the name of a king | a colour | a kind of metal
